@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+---
+id: task-001-implement-rfc-6901-json-pointer-resolvepointer
+type: task
+title: "Implement RFC 6901 JSON Pointer resolvePointer"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Implement JSON Pointer per RFC 6901, exported as `resolvePointer(document, pointer)` from
+`src/index.ts`. First of a series of features that build on each other.
+
+## What was done
+
+- Added `src/jsonPointer.ts` with the `resolvePointer` implementation:
+  - `""` resolves to the whole document.
+  - Non-empty pointers must start with `/`; otherwise throws.
+  - Reference tokens are unescaped in RFC order: `~1` → `/` first, then `~0` → `~`.
+  - Object tokens look up own properties by exact (unescaped) key; missing key throws.
+  - Array tokens must match `^(0|[1-9][0-9]*)$`; `-`, leading zeros, non-numeric tokens, and
+    out-of-range indices all throw.
+  - Stepping into a scalar (non-object, non-array) throws.
+  - A non-string `pointer` argument throws `TypeError` (input validated at the boundary).
+- `src/index.ts` re-exports `resolvePointer`.
+- Added `src/jsonPointer.test.ts` with happy-path and edge/error-path coverage (15 tests), written
+  before the implementation (red, then green).
+- Added `typescript` and `@types/node` as devDependencies; added `rewriteRelativeImportExtensions`
+  and `types: ["node"]` to `tsconfig.json` so `.ts`-suffixed relative imports (needed for Node's
+  native TypeScript execution) type-check and compile to `.js` suffixes on build.
+- Added an `npm run typecheck` script (`tsc --noEmit`) as the project's type-checking gate, since no
+  linter is configured yet.
+
+## Verification
+
+- `npm test` — 15/15 passing.
+- `npm run typecheck` — no errors.
